1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
Well, I'd like to ask you about some contingencies you're planning for, if that's OK.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:08,020
So one that you just mentioned, if all three parachutes don't open, like...

3
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,120
We can land safely with two.

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:10,900
OK.

5
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:11,340
Yeah.

6
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:19,560
But you know, it might be a little more of an impact to the crew on two parachutes, but we're landing

7
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:24,460
in water, which should help some, but definitely that's why we have three, right?

8
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:25,740
Contingency.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:33,840
We worried about, you know, making sure the vehicle, once it comes through entry, has acquired GPS

10
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:37,820
because it really orients itself to the landing location that we told it to land.

11
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:46,040
So that's why we are so far back, just in case it didn't acquire GPS, so that we don't

12
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:48,920
accidentally go to where we shouldn't be.

13
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:52,890
We develop what's called recovery decision criterias.

